      "side": 1,
      "message": "if the underlying network changes during a disconnect, is it not safe to say that the connection needs to be killed on that old underlying network and then bought back up on the new network? Not 100% clear to me how this is \"supposed\" to play out. In the \"null\" case, kill is kind of obvious, but in the non-null case, things get weird.",
